nte exploitabilité par comparaison avec la technique antérieure et convient pour diverses applications, notamment d'inspection ou de thérapie (inspection de contraste, traitement des constrictions, thérapie embolique, extraction-récupération de corps étrangers, capture de calculs, etc.).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>